0,Oto-Manguean languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oto-Manguean_languages,The Oto-Manguean or Otomanguean languages are a large family comprising several subfamilies of indigenous languages of the Americas.,"Amuzgo, Ipalapa",Otomanguean
1,Eastern Otomanguean | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/subgroup/3812/,"Eastern Otomanguean. Subgroup of 142 languages. Ancestors.Amuzgo, Ipalapa azm, a language of Mexico. Mixtecan 57. Cuicatec 2.","Amuzgo, Ipalapa",Otomanguean
2,Amuzgo | Encyclopedia.com,https://www.encyclopedia.com/humanities/encyclopedias-almanacs-transcripts-and-maps/amuzgo,"In Oaxaca, the main settlements are San Pedro Amuzgos and Santa María Ipalapa.The Amuzgo language is classified as an independent branch of the Otomanguean Language Family. Amuzgo shows dialectal differences but maintains relative mutual intelligibility.","Amuzgo, Ipalapa",Otomanguean
3,"Listing of language information for Amuzgo, Ipalapa",https://web.archive.org/web/20130827172932/http://www.ethnologue.com/language/azm,"Otomanguean, Eastern Otomanguean, Amuzgo-Mixtecan, Amuzgo. Dialects. Somewhat intelligible with other Amuzgo.OLAC resources in and about Amuzgo, Ipalapa.","Amuzgo, Ipalapa",Otomanguean
4,Otomanguean Stock,https://www.meta-religion.com/Linguistics/Languages_of_Mexico/otomanguean_stock.htm,"Amuzgo The Amuzgoan languages form one of the smallest families of the Otomanguean stock. There are three main variants of Amuzgo, spoken in the Sierra Madre del Sur near the border between the states of Guerrero and Oaxaca.","Amuzgo, Ipalapa",Otomanguean
5,"Amuzgo, Ipalapa in Mexico people group profile | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/index.php/people_groups/14741/MX,"There are three Amuzgo subgroups, each with a separate language. One of these is the Ipalapa Amuzgos. Their language is similar to the Mixtec languages; the two tribes intermingle in the states of Guerro and others. The two languages began to separate 3,000-4,000 years ago.","Amuzgo, Ipalapa",Otomanguean
6,San Pedro Amuzgos Amuzgo - azg (Otomanguean),https://peoplegroups.org/language/azg/,"Media Resources for San Pedro Amuzgos Amuzgo: JESUS – Amuzgo, Oaxaca (azg). Provided by the Jesus Film Project.","Amuzgo, Ipalapa",Otomanguean
7,(PDF) Grammatical expressions of possession in Amuzgo...,https://www.academia.edu/129166418/Grammatical_expressions_of_possession_in_Amuzgo_Otomanguean_Evidence_from_San_Pedro_Amuzgos,"This paper describes the possession of the Amuzgo of Oaxaca. A double system is distinguished: one synthetic and the other analytical. In the first, for single nominal the grammatical resources are phonological, morphological and semantic.","Amuzgo, Ipalapa",Otomanguean
8,Amuzgo language - Wikiwand,https://www.wikiwand.com/en/articles/Amuzgo_language,"Amuzgo is an Oto-Manguean language spoken in the Costa Chica region of the Mexican states of Guerrero and Oaxaca by about 60,000 speakers.","Amuzgo, Ipalapa",Otomanguean
9,Dobui | Nasal allophony and nasalization in Xochistlahuaca Amuzgo,https://www.glossa-journal.org/article/id/5434/,"This paper proposes an account of nasalization phenomena in Xochistlahuaca Amuzgo (XA), a variety of Guerrero Amuzgo, using insight from the phonology-morphology interface within the context of constraints due to monosyllabic lexical roots.","Amuzgo, Ipalapa",Otomanguean
